  "findings": [
    "Resolved White Pine–Fish Creek to its own public launch identity, with a display-only 18.95-mile river course; the old 11-mile estimate remains withheld.",
    "Added the distinct Fish Creek–Knife Edge stretch, with published guide mileage of 11.8 miles and a separately reviewed 12.10-mile generalized course.",
    "Preserved the ambiguous combined access ID as pending history; neither existing access IDs nor previously reviewed coordinates were repurposed.",
    "Wild Goose is documented but is currently seasonally closed and downstream of Lowell. It remains research only; Gateway–Lowell is still held."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Local only; not published.",
    "Access areas remain approximate and require on-site identification of the usable landing.",
    "No new GPS ETA, safe rapid line, land overlay or shoreline connector.",
    "White Pine planning distance remains under review; the dotted course does not silently restore an estimate.",
    "Gateway–Wild Goose imagery was rendered but its full course was not approved."
  ]
